```css
.circle {
  fill: radial-gradient(white, lightblue);
  filter: drop-shadow(15px 15px 15px gray) drop-shadow(-15px -15px 15px gray); // Adding a negative shadow for depth
  transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
  background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #fff, #ffcccc);
  box-shadow: 10px 10px 5px 0px rgba(0,0,0,0.75), inset 0px 0px 10px 5px rgba(255,255,255,0.5); // Adding an inner white shadow for contrast
  border-radius: 50%;
  transform: translateZ(2px); // Adding a slight z-index shift
}
```

These changes will give the circle a more pronounced 3D appearance by adding shadows on both sides, an inner contrasting shadow, and a slight z-index shift. However, keep in mind that excessive use of 3D effects may impact performance and accessibility, so consider testing it thoroughly before implementation.

