 To retrieve the username from a JSON Web Token (JWT) in an ASP.NET C# WebAPI, you can follow these steps:

First, you need to add the `Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens` NuGet package to your project if you haven't already. This package includes the necessary classes for parsing and validating JWT tokens.

```sh
Install-Package Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens
```

Next, create a helper method that extracts the username from the token:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt;

public static string GetUsernameFromJwtToken(string jwtToken)
{
    try
    {
        // Handler for JWT validation and token decoding
        JwtSecurityTokenHandler tokenHandler = new JwtSecurityTokenHandler();

        // Parse the JWT token
        JwtSecurityToken securityToken = tokenHandler.ReadJwtToken(jwtToken);

        // Retrieve the username from the claims
        return securityToken.Claims.FirstOrDefault(x => x.Type == ClaimTypes.Name)?.Value;
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        throw new ArgumentException("Invalid or expired JWT token.", nameof(jwtToken));
    }
}
```

Finally, call this helper method whenever you want to get the username from a JWT token:

```csharp
string jwtToken = Request.Headers["Authorization"].Replace("Bearer ", ""); // Assuming the token is sent as a Bearer token in the Authorization header
string username = GetUsernameFromJwtToken(jwtToken);
```

