\date{\today}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section*{Description of Issue}
We have encountered an issue with the integration of the XYZ third-party API into our multi-tiered system architecture. The error occurs when attempting to make an API call from the presentation tier to the application tier. The following error message is displayed:

\verb|Error 500: Internal Server Error|

Additionally, the application logs reveal the following error:

\verb|java.net.ConnectException: Connection refused: no further information|

\section*{System Architecture}
The following diagram illustrates our system architecture:

\begin{figure}[h!]
\centering
\begin{tikzpicture}[node distance=2cm]
\node (presentation) [rectangle] {Presentation Tier};
\node (application) [rectangle, below of=presentation, yshift=-1cm] {Application Tier};
\node (database) [rectangle, below of=application, yshift=-1cm] {Database Tier};

\draw[-] (presentation) -- (application);
\draw[-] (application) -- (database);

\node (api) [ellipse, above left of=application, xshift=-3cm, yshift=-1.5cm] {Third-Party API};

\draw[-] (application) -- (api);
\end{tikzpicture}
\caption{Multi-tiered System Architecture}
\label{fig:architecture}
\end{figure}

The integration of the third-party API is handled by the application tier using the Java HttpURLConnection class.

\section*{Proposed Solution and Timeline}
Based on our investigation, it appears that the issue may be caused by a firewall rule blocking the connection to the third-party API.

