 I'm here to help you set up Single Sign-On (SSO) with Auth0 for multiple React applications. This setup will not only make the authentication process more seamless but also enhance the security of your applications. Here's a step-by-step guide on how to do it:

**Step 1:** Create an Auth0 account
If you don't already have an Auth0 account, sign up for one at https://auth0.com/signup. After signing up, log in and create a new Application by clicking on "Applications" in the left sidebar and then "Create Application". Select "Single Page Web Applications", provide a name for your application, and add a Callback URL. Repeat these steps for each of your React applications.

**Step 2:** Install Auth0 libraries
Install the `@auth0/auth0-spa-js` library in each of your React applications using npm or yarn:

```bash
npm install @auth0/auth0-spa-js
# or
yarn add @auth0/auth0-spa-js
```

**Step 3:** Configure your applications in Auth0
In your Auth0 Dashboard, go to the "Domain" tab for each application and note down the Domain value. Add the following origins and redirect URIs for each application:

1. The base URL of your application
2. The Callback URL you specified during the application creation

**Step 4:** Initialize Auth0 in your React applications
Create an `Auth0Provider.js` file in the root directory of each application and initialize Auth0 with the Domain and Client ID obtained from the Auth0 dashboard:

```javascript
import { useAuth0 } from "@auth0/auth0-react";

export const Auth0Context = React.createContext();
export const Auth0Provider = ({ children }) => {
  const { isAuthenticated, loginWithRedirect, logout, user } = useAuth0();

  return (
    <Auth0Context.Provider
      value={{
        isAuthenticated,
        loginWithRedirect,
        logout,
        user,
      }}
    >
      {children}
    </Auth0Context.Provider>
  );
};
```

